&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lithic is the modern card issuing and processing platform empowering ambitious financial companies to build the future of payments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our infrastructure powers card programs for 100+ innovative clients, from fintechs reimagining credit and digital banking to platforms transforming disbursements and spend management. Companies like Mercury, Flex, and Novo rely on Lithic&#39;s developer-friendly APIs, direct network connections, and flawless reconciliation to launch and scale card programs in weeks, not years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building a future where access to better financial products materially improves people&#39;s lives, free from the constraints of 30-year-old mainframes and legacy processors. We&#39;re proud to be backed by world-class investors who share that vision, including Bessemer Venture Partners, Index Ventures, Spark Capital, Stripes, and Mastercard, along with many others.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a team of 170+ across 26 states and 7 countries, headquartered in New York City.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lithic&#39;s Treasury Operations team owns the movement of money across our card issuing infrastructure — network settlement, sponsor bank transfers, and the reconciliation that keeps it all provable. This is a hands-on, high-ownership role for someone who wants to learn the inner workings of payments and fintech infrastructure, not just observe them from a reporting layer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be running a critical, time-sensitive engine every day — and at the same time, working alongside the Head of Treasury Operations to improve how that engine works as the function scales. You’ll also work cross-functionally across a wide range of teams (Finance, Treasury Engineering, Risk, Analytics, Processing, Customer Success, Bank Operations) — this role sits at the center of a lot of different workflows, not off in a silo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Execution (50%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day execution of network settlement transfers (Mastercard, Visa) and related treasury transfers across sponsor banks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a time-sensitive environment where errors or delays have immediate downstream consequences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support reconciliation and ensure transfers tie out against expected activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a reliable, detail-oriented operator of an existing process — accuracy and consistency matter as much as speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Process Optimization (20%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take existing workflows and make them better: fewer manual steps, stronger controls, cleaner audit trails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify friction or risk in current processes and propose (and build) improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance improvement work against the need for strong financial controls — nothing gets streamlined at the expense of auditability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Project Support (30%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Head of Treasury Operations on larger initiatives as the function scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute analysis, documentation, and execution support to new treasury infrastructure, reporting, or process builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ongoing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run ad hoc data analysis (SQL, Excel) to answer operational and financial questions on the fly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support downstream audit and reporting needs tied to settlement and reconciliation activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be available outside normal business hours in rare emergency situations (e.g., a failed settlement or bank-side issue)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll learn:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a front-row seat to the nuts and bolts of card issuing and payments infrastructure — network settlement mechanics, sponsor bank relationships, and the guts of how money actually moves through a modern fintech stack. You&#39;ll come out of this role with a depth of operational fintech knowledge that&#39;s hard to get anywhere else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4 years of relevant experience in treasury operations, funds transfer/money movement operations, cash management, or a closely adjacent operational finance role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with reconciliation and financial controls — you understand &lt;em&gt;why&lt;/em&gt; the numbers need to tie out, not just how to make them tie out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel and Google Sheets skills, including comfort with (or willingness to learn) Google Apps Script for automating recurring workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL proficiency for querying and validating data (we use Snowflake and Metabase); Python or other scripting is a plus, not a requirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working comprehension of accounting concepts and financial operations / money movement (ACH, wires, card settlement, or similar) — you should be knowledgeable about how transfers and reconciliation tie back to the books&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Jira and Slack, or similar ticketing and collaboration tools, for tracking progress and coordinating across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort shifting flexibly between fixed process workflows and operating in an agile enrivonment (sprints, tickets, iterative process improvement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in operating in a fast-moving startup/fintech environment — this isn&#39;t a traditional back-office treasury seat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
